### S14 · práctica 1 · mismo dato, dos contratos 

@soap = https://www.dataaccess.com/webservicesserver
@api = http://localhost:8080

### 0 · Login (envíalo primero: llena {{token}})
# @name login
POST {{api}}/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{ "correo": "{{$dotenv CORREO_ENFERMERA}}", "clave": "{{$dotenv CLAVE_ENFERMERA}}" }

###
@token = {{login.response.body.data.token}}

### 1 · SOAP correcto: NumberToWords(25) → 200 con <m:NumberToWordsResult>
### (operación, parámetro ubiNum y namespace salen de {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso?WSDL)
POST {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Body>
    <NumberToWords xmlns="http://www.dataaccess.com/webservicesserver/">
      <ubiNum>25</ubiNum>
    </NumberToWords>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>

### 2 · SOAP con texto en ubiNum → este servidor NO valida el XSD: responde 200 (hallazgo)
POST {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Body>
    <NumberToWords xmlns="http://www.dataaccess.com/webservicesserver/">
      <ubiNum>quinientos</ubiNum>
    </NumberToWords>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>

### 3 · REST correcto: Mateo (id 1) → 200 con JSend success
GET {{api}}/api/pacientes/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4 · REST con error: id inexistente → 404 con JSend fail
GET {{api}}/api/pacientes/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### (extra) el WSDL completo, para la captura de la exposición
GET {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso?WSDL

### 2a · SOAP con error: operación que no existe en el WSDL → 500 con <soap:Fault>
POST {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Body>
    <NumeroAPalabras xmlns="http://www.dataaccess.com/webservicesserver/">
      <ubiNum>25</ubiNum>
    </NumeroAPalabras>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>

### 2b · SOAP con error: XML mal formado (falta cerrar ubiNum) → 500 con <soap:Fault>
POST {{soap}}/NumberConversion.wso
Content-Type: text/xml; charset=utf-8

<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<soap:Envelope xmlns:soap="http://schemas.xmlsoap.org/soap/envelope/">
  <soap:Body>
    <NumberToWords xmlns="http://www.dataaccess.com/webservicesserver/">
      <ubiNum>25
    </NumberToWords>
  </soap:Body>
</soap:Envelope>
